#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""ASUS Dial (I2C HID 0B05:0220, ProArt StudioBook) driver with on-screen menu.

The kernel creates no input device for the dial's "System Multi-Axis
Controller" collection, so we read raw reports from hidraw (id 1: byte1 bit0 =
button, bytes2-3 = int16 LE rotation, ~8-10 units per physical detent) and act on
them ourselves:

  * rotate: drives the current tool (see TOOLS); an OSD shows the result
  * short click: the tool's action (play/pause, mute, ...)
  * long press: opens the radial menu; rotate to pick a tool, then click to
    confirm (or hold, rotate and release)
"""
